@ref O 45 r 7(1) (src:6087)
GIVEN `the amount recoverable under the writ of distress has been realised by the sale of any of the movable property seized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the balance of the property seized has been released as soon as the amount was realised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the balance had been removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the balance has been returned to the premises at which the seizure was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 45 r 7(1) the balance of the property is released and returned as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the amount recoverable under the writ of distress has been realised by the sale of any of the movable property seized`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "As soon as the amount recoverable ... has been realised" -- the duty does not arise (QD)
