-- MARGINAL a | the sum of the four named amounts is the least the amount recoverable is (the Rule says "include"), not the whole | the sum is the whole amount recoverable
-- src:6087 | 7. —(1) As soon as the amount recoverable under the writ of distress has been realised by the sale of any of the movable property seized, the balance of the property seized must be released and, if it had been removed, returned to the premises at which the seizure was made. (2) The amount recoverable under the writ of distress is, for the purposes of this Rule, deemed to include the rent in respect of which the writ was issued, the expenses of the sale and of execution of the writ, the Court fees and all costs due to the landlord.
@ref O 45 r 7(2) (src:6087)
GIVEN `the rent in respect of which the writ was issued` IS A NUMBER
      `the expenses of the sale and of execution of the writ` IS A NUMBER
      `the Court fees` IS A NUMBER
      `all costs due to the landlord` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 45 r 7(2) the least the amount recoverable under the writ of distress includes` MEANS
    `the rent in respect of which the writ was issued` + `the expenses of the sale and of execution of the writ` + `the Court fees` + `all costs due to the landlord`

