-- Rule 8(1), the amount of rent: "the amount due to the landlord for the last 6 months' rent, or any less period for which rent is due".
-- The rent figures are the caller's (they come from the tenancy and the writ); the Rule fixes which period is meant: the last 6 months if rent is due for 6 months or more, otherwise the whole period for which rent is due.
-- A number, so a yes/no twin says whether the six-month limit bites, and a second twin says whether a stated amount is the amount the Rule requires.
-- src:6089 | 8. —(1) In such cases as are provided for in section 20, the Sheriff must, unless the Sheriff is already in possession under an enforcement order, deliver a copy of the writ of distress to the officer in possession under the enforcement order, and inform the officer by notice of the amount due to the landlord for the last 6 months’ rent, or any less period for which rent is due, and the amount of all fees and costs due in respect of the issue and execution of the writ of distress. (2) An application under section 20(4) to discharge or suspend the writ of distress must be made within the time and in the manner prescribed by Rule 5.
@ref O 45 r 8(1) (src:6089)
GIVEN `the case is one provided for in section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Sheriff is already in possession under an enforcement order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of months for which rent is due to the landlord` IS A NUMBER
      `the rent due to the landlord for the last 6 months` IS A NUMBER
      `the rent due to the landlord for the whole period for which rent is due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 45 r 8(1) the amount of rent to be notified to the officer` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the case is one provided for in section 20`) OR `the Sheriff is already in possession under an enforcement order`
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the amount is asked only where the duty arises; `o 45 r 8(1) the Sheriff's duty to deliver a copy of the writ and to inform the officer applies` answers JUST FALSE
           IF `the number of months for which rent is due to the landlord` AT LEAST 6
           THEN JUST `the rent due to the landlord for the last 6 months`
           IF `the number of months for which rent is due to the landlord` GREATER THAN 0
           THEN JUST `the rent due to the landlord for the whole period for which rent is due`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "or any less period for which rent is due" -- no period is one for which rent is due

-- src:6089 | 8. —(1) In such cases as are provided for in section 20, the Sheriff must, unless the Sheriff is already in possession under an enforcement order, deliver a copy of the writ of distress to the officer in possession under the enforcement order, and inform the officer by notice of the amount due to the landlord for the last 6 months’ rent, or any less period for which rent is due, and the amount of all fees and costs due in respect of the issue and execution of the writ of distress. (2) An application under section 20(4) to discharge or suspend the writ of distress must be made within the time and in the manner prescribed by Rule 5.
@ref O 45 r 8(1) (src:6089)
GIVEN `the number of months for which rent is due to the landlord` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 45 r 8(1) the rent to be notified is limited to the last 6 months` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the number of months for which rent is due to the landlord` AT LEAST 6
           THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the number of months for which rent is due to the landlord` GREATER THAN 0
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or any less period for which rent is due" -- the whole period for which rent is due is notified
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any less period for which rent is due" -- no period is one for which rent is due

-- src:6089 | 8. —(1) In such cases as are provided for in section 20, the Sheriff must, unless the Sheriff is already in possession under an enforcement order, deliver a copy of the writ of distress to the officer in possession under the enforcement order, and inform the officer by notice of the amount due to the landlord for the last 6 months’ rent, or any less period for which rent is due, and the amount of all fees and costs due in respect of the issue and execution of the writ of distress. (2) An application under section 20(4) to discharge or suspend the writ of distress must be made within the time and in the manner prescribed by Rule 5.
@ref O 45 r 8(1) (src:6089)
GIVEN `the case is one provided for in section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Sheriff is already in possession under an enforcement order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of months for which rent is due to the landlord` IS A NUMBER
      `the rent due to the landlord for the last 6 months` IS A NUMBER
      `the rent due to the landlord for the whole period for which rent is due` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of rent the Sheriff informed the officer of` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 45 r 8(1) the amount of rent notified is the amount the Rule requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 45 r 8(1) the amount of rent to be notified to the officer` `the case is one provided for in section 20` `the Sheriff is already in possession under an enforcement order` `the number of months for which rent is due to the landlord` `the rent due to the landlord for the last 6 months` `the rent due to the landlord for the whole period for which rent is due`
    WHEN JUST required THEN JUST (`the amount of rent the Sheriff informed the officer of` EQUALS required) -- the amount notified is, or is not, the amount the Rule names
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no amount is required on these facts

-- Rule 8(2): "An application under section 20(4) to discharge or suspend the writ of distress must be made within the time and in the manner prescribed by Rule 5."
-- MARGINAL a | "the time and ... the manner prescribed by Rule 5" takes in Rule 5(1) (summons, affidavit, 14 days) and Rule 5(2) (service of a copy); the results are combined: any JUST FALSE is JUST FALSE, all JUST TRUE is JUST TRUE, otherwise NOTHING | Rule 5(1) only
-- src:6089 | 8. —(1) In such cases as are provided for in section 20, the Sheriff must, unless the Sheriff is already in possession under an enforcement order, deliver a copy of the writ of distress to the officer in possession under the enforcement order, and inform the officer by notice of the amount due to the landlord for the last 6 months’ rent, or any less period for which rent is due, and the amount of all fees and costs due in respect of the issue and execution of the writ of distress. (2) An application under section 20(4) to discharge or suspend the writ of distress must be made within the time and in the manner prescribed by Rule 5.
@ref O 45 r 8(2) (src:6089)
GIVEN `the application is an application under section 20(4) to discharge or suspend the writ of distress` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds on which the application is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made on the day` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `a copy of the application and the affidavit has been served on the landlord or the landlord's agent (as the case may be)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `o 7 r 8 the day service is deemed effected` IS A DATE
      `the last day for serving the copy` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 45 r 8(2) the application is made within the time and in the manner prescribed by Rule 5` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the application is an application under section 20(4) to discharge or suspend the writ of distress`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application under section 20(4) to discharge or suspend the writ of distress"
           IF `o 45 r 5(1) the application is made as the Rule requires` TRUE `the application is made by summons` `the summons is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds on which the application is made` `the application is made on the day` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the time ... prescribed by Rule 5" (Rule 5(1): within 14 days of the seizure)
           IF `o 45 r 5(2) the copy is served as the Rule requires` `a copy of the application and the affidavit has been served on the landlord or the landlord's agent (as the case may be)` `o 7 r 8 the day service is deemed effected` `the last day for serving the copy` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the manner prescribed by Rule 5" (Rule 5(2): before the hearing)
           IF `o 45 r 5(1) the application is made as the Rule requires` TRUE `the application is made by summons` `the summons is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds on which the application is made` `the application is made on the day` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `o 45 r 5(2) the copy is served as the Rule requires` `a copy of the application and the affidavit has been served on the landlord or the landlord's agent (as the case may be)` `o 7 r 8 the day service is deemed effected` `the last day for serving the copy` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (QB); Rule 8(2) does not say what follows when the manner is not met

-- Rule 9: "Where the property seized under an enforcement order is to be released, the officer in possession under such enforcement order must, before giving up possession, notify the Sheriff of the officer's intention to do so."
-- src:6091 | 9. Where the property seized under an enforcement order is to be released, the officer in possession under such enforcement order must, before giving up possession, notify the Sheriff of the officer’s intention to do so.
@ref O 45 r 9 (src:6091)
