-- Rule 13: "Whenever the execution of a writ of distress is ordered to be suspended, unless the Court otherwise orders, any property already seized under the writ of distress remains under seizure and in the possession of the Sheriff
-- or other officer in possession; but the sale of the seized property under the writ of distress is postponed till the expiration of the period for which the execution of the writ is suspended."
-- MARGINAL b | "unless the Court otherwise orders" governs the first clause only (the nearest antecedent); the postponement of the sale is not subject to it | it governs both clauses
